{
  "chapter_id": "ncert_class9_grammar_ch4",
  "title": "Reported Speech — Direct & Indirect",
  "title_hi": "अप्रत्यक्ष कथन (Reported Speech)",
  "title_gu": "પરોક્ષ કથન (Reported Speech)",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_HOOK_1",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Step 1: Hook - The Professional Gossiper",
      "title_hi": "कदम 1: हुक - पेशेवर गपशप करने वाला (Professional Gossiper)",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 1: હૂક - વ્યાવસાયિક ગપશપ (Professional Gossiper)",
      "body": "Imagine your friend Rahul tells you a huge secret: \"I stole the principal's pen!\" The next day, you want to tell your other friend, Priya, about this. How do you say it? Do you say, \"Rahul said, 'I stole the principal's pen'\"? (This is Direct Speech—exactly quoting his words). Or do you say, \"Rahul said that he had stolen the principal's pen\"? (This is Indirect or Reported Speech). In everyday life, we are constantly 'reporting' what someone else said to another person. It's like being a professional gossiper! But to do it correctly without changing the meaning, you need to follow a few simple but strict rules of time travel and pronoun shifting.",
      "body_hi": "कल्पना कीजिए कि आपका दोस्त राहुल आपको एक बहुत बड़ा रहस्य (secret) बताता है: \"I stole the principal's pen!\" (मैंने प्रिंसिपल का पेन चुराया!) अगले दिन, आप अपने दूसरे दोस्त, प्रिया को इसके बारे में बताना चाहते हैं। आप इसे कैसे कहते हैं? क्या आप कहते हैं, \"Rahul said, 'I stole the principal's pen'\"? (यह Direct Speech है - बिल्कुल उसके शब्दों को उद्धृत / quote करना)। या आप कहते हैं, \"Rahul said that he had stolen the principal's pen\"? (यह Indirect या Reported Speech है)। रोजमर्रा की जिंदगी में, हम लगातार इस बात की 'reporting' (रिपोर्टिंग) कर रहे हैं कि किसी ने दूसरे व्यक्ति से क्या कहा। यह एक पेशेवर गपशप करने वाले (gossiper) होने जैसा है! लेकिन अर्थ को बदले बिना इसे सही ढंग से करने के लिए, आपको समय यात्रा और सर्वनाम (pronoun) परिवर्तन के कुछ सरल लेकिन सख्त नियमों का पालन करने की आवश्यकता है।",
      "body_gu": "કલ્પના કરો કે તમારો મિત્ર રાહુલ તમને એક મોટું રહસ્ય (secret) કહે છે: \"I stole the principal's pen!\" (મેં આચાર્યની પેન ચોરી લીધી!) બીજા દિવસે, તમે તમારા અન્ય મિત્ર, પ્રિયાને આ વિશે જણાવવા માંગો છો. તમે તે કેવી રીતે કહેશો? શું તમે કહો છો, \"Rahul said, 'I stole the principal's pen'\"? (આ Direct Speech છે - બરાબર તેના શબ્દો ટાંકીને / quote). અથવા તમે કહો છો, \"Rahul said that he had stolen the principal's pen\"? (આ Indirect અથવા Reported Speech છે). રોજિંદા જીવનમાં, આપણે સતત 'reporting' (રિપોર્ટિંગ) કરીએ છીએ કે અન્ય વ્યક્તિએ બીજી વ્યક્તિને શું કહ્યું. તે વ્યાવસાયિક ગપશપ (gossiper) બનવા જેવું છે! પરંતુ અર્થ બદલ્યા વિના તેને યોગ્ય રીતે કરવા માટે, તમારે સમયની મુસાફરી અને સર્વનામ (pronoun) સ્થળાંતરના થોડા સરળ પરંતુ કડક નિયમોનું પાલન કરવાની જરૂર છે."
    },
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_SOCRATIC_1",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Step 2: Socratic Thinking",
      "title_hi": "कदम 2: सुकराती सोच",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 2: સોક્રેટિક વિચાર",
      "body": "Look at this Direct Speech sentence:\nHe said to me, \"**I** am doing **my** homework **now**.\"\n\nIf you want to report this to someone else the *next day*, how does it change? \nDoes 'I' stay 'I'? No, because YOU didn't say it, 'HE' did. So 'I' becomes 'he'. \nDoes 'am doing' stay present tense? No, because he said it in the past. So 'am doing' becomes 'was doing'. \nDoes 'now' stay 'now'? No, because it was yesterday! So 'now' becomes 'then'. \n\nSo it becomes: He told me that **he** was doing **his** homework **then**. \nCan you see how reporting a speech is like acting as a translator for time and people?",
      "body_hi": "इस Direct Speech वाक्य को देखें:\nHe said to me, \"**I** am doing **my** homework **now**.\"\n\nयदि आप *अगले दिन* किसी और को इसकी रिपोर्ट करना चाहते हैं, तो यह कैसे बदलता है?\nक्या 'I' (मैं), 'I' ही रहता है? नहीं, क्योंकि आपने यह नहीं कहा, 'HE' (उसने) ने कहा। इसलिए 'I', 'he' बन जाता है।\nक्या 'am doing' (कर रहा हूँ) वर्तमान काल रहता है? नहीं, क्योंकि उसने इसे अतीत (past) में कहा था। इसलिए 'am doing', 'was doing' (कर रहा था) बन जाता है।\nक्या 'now' (अभी) 'now' रहता है? नहीं, क्योंकि वह कल था! इसलिए 'now', 'then' (तब) बन जाता है।\n\nतो यह बन जाता है: He told me that **he** was doing **his** homework **then**.\nक्या आप देख सकते हैं कि किसी भाषण की रिपोर्टिंग करना समय और लोगों के लिए अनुवादक (translator) के रूप में कार्य करने जैसा है?",
      "body_gu": "આ Direct Speech વાક્ય જુઓ:\nHe said to me, \"**I** am doing **my** homework **now**.\"\n\nજો તમે આની જાણ કોઈ અન્ય વ્યક્તિને *આગલા દિવસે* કરવા માંગતા હો, તો તે કેવી રીતે બદલાય છે?\nશું 'I' (હું), 'I' રહે છે? ના, કારણ કે તમે તે કહ્યું નથી, 'HE' (તેણે) કહ્યું છે. તેથી 'I', 'he' બની જાય છે.\nશું 'am doing' (કરી રહ્યો છું) વર્તમાન કાળ રહે છે? ના, કારણ કે તેણે તે ભૂતકાળમાં (past) કહ્યું હતું. તેથી 'am doing', 'was doing' (કરી રહ્યો હતો) બની જાય છે.\nશું 'now' (હવે) 'now' રહે છે? ના, કારણ કે તે ગઈકાલની વાત હતી! તેથી 'now', 'then' (ત્યારે) બની જાય છે.\n\nતેથી તે બની જાય છે: He told me that **he** was doing **his** homework **then**.\nશું તમે જોઈ શકો છો કે કેવી રીતે ભાષણની જાણ કરવી એ સમય અને લોકો માટે અનુવાદક (translator) તરીકે કામ કરવા સમાન છે?"
    },
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_DISCOVERY_1",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Step 3: Discovery - The Golden Rules of Transformation",
      "title_hi": "कदम 3: खोज - परिवर्तन के सुनहरे नियम",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 3: શોધ - પરિવર્તનના સુવર્ણ નિયમો",
      "body": "To convert Direct Speech to Indirect Speech, you must follow three golden rules:\n\n**Rule 1: Remove the Quotes and add 'that' (for statements)**\nDirect: She said, \"I am happy.\"\nIndirect: She said **that** she was happy.\n\n**Rule 2: Change the Pronouns**\nThe pronouns inside the quotes change according to the speaker. First Person (I, we, my) changes according to the Subject. Second Person (You, your) changes according to the Object.\n\n**Rule 3: Backshift the Tense**\nIf the reporting verb (e.g., 'said') is in the past tense, the tense inside the quotes takes one step back into the past.\n- Simple Present ➔ Simple Past\n- Present Continuous ➔ Past Continuous\n- Present Perfect ➔ Past Perfect\n- Simple Past ➔ Past Perfect\n- 'will/shall/can/may' ➔ 'would/should/could/might'",
      "body_hi": "Direct Speech को Indirect Speech में बदलने के लिए, आपको तीन सुनहरे नियमों का पालन करना होगा:\n\n**नियम 1: उद्धरण (Quotes) हटाएं और 'that' जोड़ें (कथनों के लिए)**\nDirect: She said, \"I am happy.\"\nIndirect: She said **that** she was happy.\n\n**नियम 2: सर्वनाम (Pronouns) बदलें**\nउद्धरणों के अंदर के सर्वनाम वक्ता के अनुसार बदलते हैं। प्रथम पुरुष (First Person - I, we, my) कर्ता (Subject) के अनुसार बदलता है। द्वितीय पुरुष (Second Person - You, your) कर्म (Object) के अनुसार बदलता है।\n\n**नियम 3: काल को पीछे धकेलें (Backshift the Tense)**\nयदि रिपोर्टिंग क्रिया (जैसे, 'said') भूतकाल में है, तो उद्धरणों के अंदर का काल अतीत में एक कदम पीछे (backshift) चला जाता है।\n- Simple Present ➔ Simple Past\n- Present Continuous ➔ Past Continuous\n- Present Perfect ➔ Past Perfect\n- Simple Past ➔ Past Perfect\n- 'will/shall/can/may' ➔ 'would/should/could/might'",
      "body_gu": "Direct Speech ને Indirect Speech માં રૂપાંતરિત કરવા માટે, તમારે ત્રણ સુવર્ણ નિયમોનું પાલન કરવું આવશ્યક છે:\n\n**નિયમ 1: અવતરણો (Quotes) દૂર કરો અને 'that' ઉમેરો (નિવેદનો માટે)**\nDirect: She said, \"I am happy.\"\nIndirect: She said **that** she was happy.\n\n**નિયમ 2: સર્વનામ (Pronouns) બદલો**\nઅવતરણની અંદરના સર્વનામો વક્તા મુજબ બદલાય છે. પ્રથમ પુરુષ (First Person - I, we, my) વિષય (Subject) અનુસાર બદલાય છે. બીજો પુરુષ (Second Person - You, your) પદાર્થ (Object) અનુસાર બદલાય છે.\n\n**નિયમ 3: કાળને પાછળ ખસેડો (Backshift the Tense)**\nજો રિપોર્ટિંગ ક્રિયાપદ (દા.ત., 'said') ભૂતકાળમાં હોય, તો અવતરણની અંદરનો કાળ ભૂતકાળમાં એક પગલું પાછળ (backshift) લે છે.\n- Simple Present ➔ Simple Past\n- Present Continuous ➔ Past Continuous\n- Present Perfect ➔ Past Perfect\n- Simple Past ➔ Past Perfect\n- 'will/shall/can/may' ➔ 'would/should/could/might'"
    },
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_REVEAL_1",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Step 4: Reveal - Time and Place Words",
      "title_hi": "कदम 4: प्रकट - समय और स्थान के शब्द (Time and Place Words)",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 4: પ્રગટ - સમય અને સ્થળના શબ્દો (Time and Place Words)",
      "body": "Because the reporting happens at a *different time* and often a *different place*, the words indicating time and place must also change. This is crucial for making sense!\n\n**Time & Place Shifts:**\n- now ➔ then\n- here ➔ there\n- this / these ➔ that / those\n- today ➔ that day\n- tonight ➔ that night\n- tomorrow ➔ the next day (or the following day)\n- yesterday ➔ the previous day (or the day before)\n\n**Example Transformation:**\nDirect: Ali said, \"I will buy **this** book **tomorrow**.\"\nIndirect: Ali said that he **would** buy **that** book **the next day**.\nNotice how 'will' became 'would', 'this' became 'that', and 'tomorrow' became 'the next day'!",
      "body_hi": "चूंकि रिपोर्टिंग एक *अलग समय* और अक्सर *अलग स्थान* पर होती है, इसलिए समय और स्थान को इंगित करने वाले शब्दों को भी बदलना चाहिए। समझदारी के लिए यह महत्वपूर्ण है!\n\n**समय और स्थान परिवर्तन (Time & Place Shifts):**\n- now (अब) ➔ then (तब)\n- here (यहाँ) ➔ there (वहाँ)\n- this / these (यह/ये) ➔ that / those (वह/वे)\n- today (आज) ➔ that day (उस दिन)\n- tonight (आज रात) ➔ that night (उस रात)\n- tomorrow (कल) ➔ the next day (अगले दिन)\n- yesterday (बीता हुआ कल) ➔ the previous day (पिछले दिन)\n\n**उदाहरण परिवर्तन:**\nDirect: Ali said, \"I **will** buy **this** book **tomorrow**.\"\nIndirect: Ali said that he **would** buy **that** book **the next day**.\nध्यान दें कि कैसे 'will', 'would' बन गया, 'this', 'that' बन गया, और 'tomorrow', 'the next day' बन गया!",
      "body_gu": "કારણ કે રિપોર્ટિંગ *અલગ સમયે* અને વારંવાર *અલગ સ્થળે* થાય છે, સમય અને સ્થળ દર્શાવતા શબ્દો પણ બદલાવા જોઈએ. સમજણ બનાવવા માટે આ નિર્ણાયક છે!\n\n**સમય અને સ્થળ પરિવર્તન (Time & Place Shifts):**\n- now (હવે) ➔ then (ત્યારે)\n- here (અહીં) ➔ there (ત્યાં)\n- this / these (આ) ➔ that / those (તે / પેલા)\n- today (આજે) ➔ that day (તે દિવસે)\n- tonight (આજની રાત) ➔ that night (તે રાત્રે)\n- tomorrow (આવતીકાલ) ➔ the next day (બીજા દિવસે)\n- yesterday (ગઈકાલ) ➔ the previous day (આગલા દિવસે)\n\n**ઉદાહરણ પરિવર્તન:**\nDirect: Ali said, \"I **will** buy **this** book **tomorrow**.\"\nIndirect: Ali said that he **would** buy **that** book **the next day**.\nનોંધ લો કે કેવી રીતે 'will', 'would' બન્યું, 'this', 'that' બન્યું અને 'tomorrow', 'the next day' બન્યું!"
    },
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_KNOWLEDGE_1",
      "type": "mcq",
      "title": "Step 5: Knowledge Check",
      "title_hi": "कदम 5: ज्ञान जांच",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 5: જ્ઞાન તપાસ",
      "question": "Choose the correct Indirect Speech for: She said, \"I am reading a book today.\"",
      "question_hi": "वाक्य के लिए सही Indirect Speech चुनें: She said, \"I am reading a book today.\"",
      "question_gu": "વાક્ય માટે યોગ્ય Indirect Speech પસંદ કરો: She said, \"I am reading a book today.\"",
      "options": [
        "She said that she is reading a book today.",
        "She said that she was reading a book that day.",
        "She said that I was reading a book today.",
        "She said that she was reading a book today."
      ],
      "options_hi": [
        "She said that she is reading a book today. (गलत - Tense और 'today' नहीं बदला)",
        "She said that she was reading a book that day. (सही - Tense बदला, Pronoun बदला, 'today' बदला)",
        "She said that I was reading a book today. (गलत - Pronoun 'I' नहीं बदला)",
        "She said that she was reading a book today. (गलत - 'today' नहीं बदला)"
      ],
      "options_gu": [
        "She said that she is reading a book today. (ખોટું - Tense અને 'today' બદલાયા નથી)",
        "She said that she was reading a book that day. (સાચું - Tense બદલાયો, Pronoun બદલાયો, 'today' બદલાયો)",
        "She said that I was reading a book today. (ખોટું - Pronoun 'I' બદલાયો નથી)",
        "She said that she was reading a book today. (ખોટું - 'today' બદલાયો નથી)"
      ],
      "correct_index": 1,
      "explanation": "To change to Indirect Speech: \n1. Add 'that'. \n2. Change 'I' to 'she' (matching the speaker).\n3. Backshift the tense 'am reading' (Present Continuous) to 'was reading' (Past Continuous).\n4. Change 'today' to 'that day'. \nResult: She said that she was reading a book that day.",
      "explanation_hi": "Indirect Speech में बदलने के लिए:\n1. 'that' जोड़ें।\n2. 'I' को 'she' में बदलें (वक्ता से मिलान करते हुए)।\n3. 'am reading' (Present Continuous) काल को 'was reading' (Past Continuous) में पीछे धकेलें।\n4. 'today' को 'that day' में बदलें।\nपरिणाम: She said that she was reading a book that day.",
      "explanation_gu": "Indirect Speech માં બદલવા માટે:\n1. 'that' ઉમેરો.\n2. 'I' ને 'she' માં બદલો (સ્પીકર સાથે મેચિંગ).\n3. 'am reading' (Present Continuous) કાળને 'was reading' (Past Continuous) પર પાછા ખસેડો.\n4. 'today' ને 'that day' માં બદલો.\nપરિણામ: She said that she was reading a book that day."
    },
    {
      "id": "CBSE_9_GRAMMAR_CH4_REFLECTION_1",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Step 6: Reflection",
      "title_hi": "कदम 6: प्रतिबिंब",
      "title_gu": "પગલું 6: પ્રતિબિંબ",
      "body": "When you report someone else's speech, you are essentially telling a story about the past. That is why we usually take the tense one step back into the past (Present becomes Past). You also have to adjust the perspective (I becomes He/She) because YOU are the one talking now, not them. But be careful of the one big exception! If a statement is a universal truth, you DON'T backshift the tense. \nExample: The teacher said, \"The Earth is round.\" \nIndirect: The teacher said that the Earth IS round. (Because it is STILL round today!). \nMastering these small shifts makes you a clear and accurate communicator.",
      "body_hi": "जब आप किसी और के भाषण (speech) की रिपोर्ट करते हैं, तो आप अनिवार्य रूप से अतीत (past) के बारे में एक कहानी बता रहे होते हैं। यही कारण है कि हम आम तौर पर काल (tense) को एक कदम पीछे अतीत में ले जाते हैं (वर्तमान काल, भूतकाल बन जाता है)। आपको परिप्रेक्ष्य (perspective) को भी समायोजित करना होगा (मैं, वह बन जाता है) क्योंकि अब आप बात कर रहे हैं, वे नहीं। लेकिन एक बड़े अपवाद (exception) से सावधान रहें! यदि कोई कथन एक सार्वभौमिक सत्य (universal truth) है, तो आप काल को पीछे (backshift) नहीं करते हैं।\nउदाहरण: The teacher said, \"The Earth is round.\"\nIndirect: The teacher said that the Earth IS round. (क्योंकि यह आज भी गोल है!)।\nइन छोटे बदलावों में महारत हासिल करना आपको एक स्पष्ट और सटीक कम्युनिकेटर बनाता है।",
      "body_gu": "જ્યારે તમે કોઈ અન્યના ભાષણની (speech) જાણ કરો છો, ત્યારે તમે અનિવાર્યપણે ભૂતકાળ (past) વિશે વાર્તા કહી રહ્યા છો. તેથી જ આપણે સામાન્ય રીતે કાળને એક પગલું ભૂતકાળમાં લઈ જઈએ છીએ (વર્તમાન, ભૂતકાળ બની જાય છે). તમારે પરિપ્રેક્ષ્યને (perspective) પણ સમાયોજિત કરવું પડશે (હું, તે/તેણી બની જાય છે) કારણ કે તમે અત્યારે વાત કરી રહ્યાં છો, તેઓ નહીં. પરંતુ એક મોટા અપવાદથી (exception) સાવચેત રહો! જો વિધાન સાર્વત્રિક સત્ય (universal truth) છે, તો તમે કાળને પાછળ ખસેડતા (backshift) નથી.\nઉદાહરણ: The teacher said, \"The Earth is round.\"\nIndirect: The teacher said that the Earth IS round. (કારણ કે તે આજે પણ ગોળ છે!).\nઆ નાના ફેરફારોમાં નિપુણતા મેળવવી તમને સ્પષ્ટ અને સચોટ વાતચીત કરનાર બનાવે છે."
    }
  ]
}